==Description==

Increases pet ability power depending on pet level and pet playtime. Can utilize three different modes, which augment his ability to charge spells, stack buffs, or use profiting spells.

Unique [[Sources|Source]]: Grim Trophy, replacing Enchanted Tree.

In addition, Oni has access to Hellholes (instead of Circles of Power) and Monuments (instead of Spell Fountains), like the {{ClassTooltip|Demonologist}} and the {{ClassTooltip|Ironsoul}}.

Upon reaching [[Paragon]] 42, Oni may take on either [[Ascension Forms]]: {{ClassTooltip|Tempest}} or {{ClassTooltip|Defiance}}.

==Basic Design==
{{ClassTooltip|class_name = Oni}} is a combination of {{ClassTooltip|class_name = Ironsoul}} and {{ClassTooltip|class_name = Demonologist}} and thus combines high pet levels and well scaling accumalated spells, such as {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Enhanced Strength}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Iron Blood}}. Oni also synergizes well with high pet levels with the spell {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Possessed Blade}} and it's hero abilities both scaling with PetLevel^0.8.

Since Oni has access to {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Furious Strike}} you can use {{ItemTooltip|item_name = Berzerker}} to stack spells, Oni's defense stance also gives you the ability to greatly increase casts per second even without {{ItemTooltip|item_name = Berzerker}}.

While bursting Oni commonly uses {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Iron Blood}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Enhanced Strength}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Possessed Blade}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Ritual Of Power}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Goblet Of Fire}} and uses the evocation spell {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Furious Strike}}. {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Furious Strike}} can be charged using {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Temper The Steel}}. The more charges, the more profit.

This makes for a long-term scaling class with a lot of pet levels.

